{
  "title": "The Final Outlaw",
  "short_description": "Ride a trail of 100 desert challenges, then face an endless frontier.",
  "long_description": "One trail. A hundred last stands.\n\nThe Final Outlaw is a portrait top-down frontier monster shooter with 100 campaign stages and endless survival. Fight through ten districts of handcrafted street plans: adobe houses, narrow alleys, road junctions and cover make each saved town a different encounter.\n\nMove with your left thumb and hold the gun control to fire. Assisted targeting follows a visible foe, but every shot is your decision. Your starting magazine holds 20 rounds. Reload deliberately, watch the ammo counter and dash out of danger.\n\nFast fragile runners, heavy tanks, ranged attackers and guardians route around town obstacles. Clear encounters, survive the clock, gather supplies, hold your ground or defeat a guardian. Earn campaign stars, experience and equipment between attempts.\n\nSeven permanent gear tracks improve damage, health, movement speed, magazine capacity, reload speed, dash recovery and armor. Daily quests and a seven-day gift streak offer more progress. Core play and progression save locally and work offline.\n\nAndroid supports an optional earned continue after a loss, supply rewards and ads at between-round breaks. A continue is granted only after the earned callback and gameplay waits behind the ad endcard. Google Play Games achievements and leaderboards require sign-in and the owner's final backend configuration. The Web edition keeps local play with graceful Android-service fallbacks.",
